NAME: CRM sweep
OWNER: CRM & Reactivation
ACCOUNT: business
WHEN: Every weekday at 5:31 AM (Australia/Brisbane)
MILESTONE: M3
STATUS: Created paused. Turned on only after Tommy says yes.
---
Switch check: read /workspace/tmec-team/context/routines-on.md. If "CRM sweep" isn't listed there as "on" or "test", append "<time> · CRM sweep · SKIPPED_OFF" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md and stop.
Test mode: if it's listed as "test", send every message to the owner only (Tommy, or Justin's team in a test run), never to a channel or anyone else, and start each message with "TEST". Write state only under /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/, never the live sent keys, alert flags or data files.
Stop check: if /workspace/tmec-team/state/EXTERNAL_WRITES_STOPPED exists, append "<time> · CRM sweep · SKIPPED_STOPPED" to the run log and stop, sending nothing. The one exception: pause or unschedule your own already-scheduled sends, as your skill's stop section says. Whoever stopped the team already told Tommy.
Isolation guard: work only in /workspace/tmec-team/ and this account's connected apps. If /workspace/tmec-team/context/owner.md is missing, append "<time> · CRM sweep · NO_CLIENT_SOURCE" to the run log and stop. Read other bots' files only where your skill says so; never write them, and never use another bot's logins or memory.
Lean run: read only what this job needs. Stop with NO_CHANGE only where the job below says nothing changed: append "<time> · CRM sweep · NO_CHANGE" to the run log and stop. A report that always goes out never stops here.
Run log: when you finish, append "<time> · CRM sweep · EXECUTED · <one-line result>" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md, or FAILED with the reason. A source you couldn't read is UNKNOWN in your output, never zero.

First, read your decisions: for each file in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/decisions/crm-reactivation/ that isn't in /workspace/tmec-team/state/sent-keys-crm-reactivation.md yet, act on it by its id: an add- id with the crm-sweep skill (recompute the hash from the pending payload and match it to the decision's; a yes is marked "approved, Tommy to pass to Alfred", because you never write HubSpot contacts or deals; a no is declined; a change is redrafted once as a new item); a qq- id with the quiet-quote-followup skill's step "Act on a decision" (the send gate applies: stop file absent, not test mode and config.json run is tommy, live_sends true, hash recomputed and matching, id not in the sent keys); a react- id is left for the reactivation-batch routine. Add every handled id and its outcome to the sent keys, so a no or a change is never read again. TMEC Command may already have nudged you to act in your own chat; this is the fallback. In test mode (this routine is listed test, or config.json run is test), write what you would have done to /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/ and do nothing outward, make no treg call, and start item ids with test-.
Stop exception: if the stop file exists, the stop check above applies in full except for one action it doesn't forbid because it only removes a send: before you end the run, unschedule every REACT-QQ- email you scheduled that hasn't sent yet, and list in the daily note anything you couldn't unschedule.
Then read any new job in /workspace/tmec-team/requests/to-crm-reactivation/ and do it first.
Then use the crm-sweep skill: read HubSpot (read-only), find the follow-ups due, quotes nobody chased, replies waiting and deals gone quiet, copy new unsubscribes (including "for CRM & Reactivation" lines from the partner bots) into /workspace/tmec-team/data/crm/suppression.csv, read the radar hand-off files and Dream 100's tagged partner hand-off files (/workspace/tmec-team/data/partners/handoff/*.jsonl), list any new buyers or enquiries that aren't in HubSpot yet as one "add to HubSpot" item for Tommy to pass to Alfred (people with contact details, and a separate section for radar leads with no contact details: platform, handle, post link, area, what they asked, the drafted reply), and write tagged won deals to /workspace/tmec-team/data/crm/partner-sales.md.
Then use the quiet-quote-followup skill: for quotes that went quiet and are due a step in the six-email sequence, draft the emails (to a limit of 25) and put them in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/pending/crm-reactivation/ as one batch item (qq-, in the item format with the list file's hash). Drafting sends or schedules nothing.
If HubSpot can't be read, write "UNKNOWN: HubSpot" in the daily note, never "all clear". If nothing changed since the last run (no new item, no new radar file, no decision, no new quiet quote), write NO_CHANGE and stop.
Mondays are Tommy's meeting day: anything for him from this run is marked "show Tuesday".
Write /workspace/tmec-team/daily/<today>/crm-reactivation.md (on a Wednesday the reactivation batch routine writes the same note: if it already exists, append a section and never overwrite it): counts and HubSpot record ids only (never an email address or phone number), what needs Tommy, anything blocked and why, and "Source: HubSpot, read <time>".
